            <ArticleTitle>Inflammatory myofibroblastic tumor of the midesophagus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>243-54</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/15513810801893421</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An inflammatory myofibroblastic tumor (IMFT) is a rare entity that can arise in a multiplicity of organs including the lung, liver, and at any location within the gastrointestinal tract. Typically, an IMFT presents as a localized mass with clinical symptoms dependent upon its site of origin. IMFTs pathologically resemble a neoplastic process but are theorized to arise from an unknown inflammatory event. We present a case of a midesophageal IMFT in a 12-year-old female.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
